ng\nMasters in CIS Thesis and Non-Thesis Options\nTransfer Students\nTour the College\nSelective Admission\nAbout\nFaculty and Staff\nIn the News\nAdvisory Board\nContact Us\nStudent Resources\nFAQ\nPolicies\nForms\nTutors\nLabs and Equipment\nComputer Recommendations\nResearch\nQuantum Computing\nHuman-Centered Computing\nCyber Security\nCloud Computing\nArtificial Intelligence\nFL-DSSG\nPolicies and Forms\nPolicies\nForms\noneColumn\nSchool of Computing Graduate Programs\nDoctor of Philosophy\nAt the University of North Florida, a Ph.D. in Computing is more than an academic pursuit\u2014it\u2019s a hands-on exploration. UNF\u2019s professors are seasoned researchers who guide you through rigorous projects, from Intelligent Systems to Cybersecurity. Their mentorship is grounded in real-world challenges. Whether you aspire to impact academia, industry, or government, a UNF Ph.D. equips you. You will publish, present, and innovate\u2014preparing for an exciting career. So, if you seek practical research, community impact, and a supportive academic environment, UNF awaits.\nLearn More\nMaster of Science; Computing and Information Sciences\nMS CIS - Thesis Option\nThe M.S.-CIS (Thesis) requires a total of 30 graduate credit hours, of which 24 credit hours must be earned through coursework. The student must enroll in the graduate Thesis course for at least two semesters, which requires conducting an in-depth study of a research problem leading to the composition of a Master's Thesis that summarizes the student\u2019s findings. The student must defend the thesis in a presentation that is open to the general public and evaluated by a faculty committee.\nArtificial Intelligence\nComputer Science\nCybersecurity\nData Science\nInformation Systems\nArtificial Intelligence\nComputer Science\nCybersecurity\nData Science\nInformation Systems\nMS CIS - Non-Thesis Option\nThe MS-CIS, (Non-Thesis), requires a total of 30 graduate credit hours, of which 24 credit hours must be earned through coursework. The student must enroll in the graduate Research Experience I & & II courses. During the Research Experience, the student is required to submit a manuscript to a journal or conference proceedings or submit a grant proposal to an external funding agency.\nArtificial Intelligence\nComputer Science\nCybersecurity\nData Science\nInformation Systems\nArtificial Intelligence\nComputer Science\nCybersecurity\nData Science\nInformation Systems\nContact Us\nSOCGraduatePrograms@unf.edu | (904) 620-2985\nApply Now\nContact your Advisor\n(904) 620-STEM\nccecadvising@unf.edu\nCollege of Computing, Engineering and Construction\n1 UNF Drive\nSkinner - Jones Hall\nBuilding 4 STE. 4201\nJacksonville, FL 32224\n(904) 620-1350\nGeneral Information: ccec.info@unf.edu\nContact Us\nView Map\nUNF Central\nDirectory\nEmergency\nPrivacy\nRegulations\nConsumer Information\nStudent Achievement\nDisability Accommodations\nReport a Concern\nClery Act\nTitle IX\nJobs at UNF\nIf you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the site due to a disability, visit our\nwebsite accessibility page.", "links": [["Skip to Main Content", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/computing/Graduate-Programs.html#mainContent"], ["", "https://www.unf.edu"], ["A-Z Index", "https://www.unf.edu/sitemap/"], ["", "https://www.unf.edu/search/"], ["College of Computing, Engineering and Construction", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/"], ["Academics", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/computing/Graduate-Programs.html"], ["School of Computing", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/computing/index.html"], ["School of Engineering", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/engineering/index.html"], ["Construction Management", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/construction/index.html"], ["Outreach", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/computing/Graduate-Programs.html"], ["Home", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/outreach/index.html"], ["Our Mission", "https://www.unf.edu/ccec/outreach/mission.html"], ["K-12 STEM Hub", "https://stem2hub.org/  "], ["Advising", "https://www